fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: boranis_honor_guard
name: Boranis Honor Guard
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  level: 3
  role: standard
  armor: 1
  morale: 10
  weapon: "House blade"
  wants: >
    The room held and the offender out of it — detained and expelled, never
    killed.
  special: >
    WARDER — each honor guard carries two charged house crystals (a seal and a
    flare) and knows the palace's ward-points by heart. Once per scene a guard
    fires one instead of attacking: a door seals across the party's way out,
    or a flare lights the corridor so that nobody in it can hide.
  when_bloodied: >
    Falls back to the nearest ward-point and calls out. Four more honor guards
    are two exchanges away, and this one holds until they come.
  tells: >
    Glances at the nearest ward-point before moving; touches the crystal at the
    belt before firing it. A guard who turns his back to the palace doors has
    stopped detaining and started defending.
  breaks: >
    Never flees the house. Broken, a guard steps back, lowers the blade and
    offers terms: surrender, and the evening ends in the gatehouse cell.
  twists:
  - "A second guard arrives from the far end, and the way back is shut."
  - "The guard fires a seal: the nearest door grows shut, and everyone on the wrong side of it is somewhere else now."
  - "The guard fires a flare. Every face in the corridor is lit, and everyone will be remembered."
  - "Corval's voice from down the hall asks what is going on, in the tone of a man who will find out."
  - "A guest stumbles into the middle of it, masked and appalled, and has to be got out of the way."
  - "The guard names the offender's house aloud. Whatever happens next, the room knows who it was."
  description: >
    One of the nine. The Boranis honor guard should number forty at an event
    like this; the nine on duty tonight are the ones Raunu judged he could not
    make leave, and they stand facing the palace doors, not the gates. Veterans
    to the last, courteous to guests, and entirely without illusions about
    what they signed up for — though even they do not know what is actually
    coming.
  notes: >
    Use this card if players cross the house itself: forcing the east wing,
    robbing the trophy gallery loudly, or refusing the gatehouse cell. Honor
    guards fight to detain and expel, and they are good enough that a starting
    party should feel it. A player character they drop to 0 HP is held, not
    hurt worse: take the Wound, and Hold On can go no lower than 7–9. Surrender
    costs the evening — mask, invitation, and the rest of the night in the
    gatehouse cell — and not the character.

    AT MIDNIGHT they die or fall protecting their chief — quickly, around the
    edges of the frame (module Chapter V). That outcome is scripted regardless
    of these numbers; the card exists for the hours before the bells, or for
    tables whose plans put them beside the nine when the lights die.
  organization: >
    Nine on the night of the ball, placed inward, facing the palace doors.
  reskin_of: null
created_at: '2026-07-12T00:00:00+00:00'
last_modified: '2026-09-25T00:00:00+00:00'
